diff --git a/lib/nvme/host_saps.c b/lib/nvme/host_saps.c
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..2ea0e6381
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/nvme/host_saps.c
@@ -0,0 +1,2298 @@
+/* Phase A — Host-only SAPS classifier (mode b).
+ *
+ * Bit-for-bit port of the DPA-resident classifier in
+ * dpa-smart-initiator/.../dpa_plugin/dev/dpa_plugin_dev.c.
+ *
+ * Differences from the DPA source:
+ *   * FlexIO intrinsics (flexio_dev_print, dpa polling) removed — algorithm
+ *     runs synchronously inside nvme_rdma.c hooks.
+ *   * Shared ring storage replaced with static host arrays:
+ *       g_host_saps_path_score[qp][path]         (read by bdev_nvme selector)
+ *       g_host_saps_path_state[qp][path]         (monitoring)
+ *       g_host_saps_path_retry_verdict[qp][path] (read by retry overlay)
+ *   * No producer/consumer ring — saps_update() is called directly from the
+ *     submit/complete hook (no batching, no fence).
+ *   * ctrlr→path_idx kept atomic+per-thread-cached so multiple SPDK reactors
+ *     (one per core) can resolve the same controller pointer without races.
+ *   * spdk_get_ticks() (in nvme_rdma.c) provides host TSC; algorithm uses it
+ *     directly (same monotonic clock domain — DPA TSC was 1.5 GHz, host TSC
+ *     is platform-dependent so SAPS_TICKS_PER_MS is recomputed at init from
+ *     spdk_get_ticks_hz()).
+ *
+ * Numeric tunables (NEWMA λ_fast/λ_slow/H, Frugal-2U PRNG threshold, FSM
+ * thresholds, hysteresis N, score weights, BIMODAL shift, …) are KEPT
+ * IDENTICAL to dpa_plugin_dev.c so mode (b) vs mode (c) ablation isolates
+ * "DPA hardware vs host CPU" rather than "different algorithm constants".
+ *
+ * Footprint:
+ *   g_host_saps_path[CONN_MAX=1024][PATH_MAX=4] × ~512 B per state ≈ 2 MiB
+ *   g_host_saps_path_score    [1024][4] × 4 B = 16 KiB
+ *   g_host_saps_path_state    [1024][4] × 2 B =  8 KiB
